// D2445: a 700-term `+` chain classifies its operand width once per node. Every operator's
// emission asks the width of its operands, and that answer re-walked the whole left subtree at
// every level, so the compiler's cost was cubic in the chain and trapped past about 600 terms.
// The chain keeps its memo as the operand of a comparison, a condition or a `&&`.
